ExactFillSettler_fill
├── when block.timestamp is greater than order.fillDeadline
│   └── it should revert with FillAfterDeadline
├── when orderStatus is Settled or Refunded or Cancelled
│   └── it should revert with OrderInTerminalState
├── when orderData.allowPartialFills is true
│   └── it should revert with InconsistentIntent
├── when orderData.srcCstToken equals orderData.premiumToken
│   └── it should revert with InvalidOrderTokenPair
├── when orderData.exclusiveFiller is set AND msg.sender is not that address
│   └── it should revert with NotExclusiveFiller
├── when orderData.exclusiveFiller is set AND msg.sender is that address
│   └── it should accept the fill
├── when orderData.minFillSize is non-zero AND rollover output.amount is less than minFillSize
│   └── it should revert with BelowMinFillSize
├── when orderData.minFillSize is non-zero AND rollover output.amount equals orderSize
│   └── it should accept the fill
├── when orderData.minFillSize is non-zero AND caller fills the premium leg with premium output.amount below minFillSize
│   └── it should admit the premium leg (AS-19 is rollover-leg only)
├── when collateralAsset decimals are 6 AND rollover output.amount is aligned to the decimal offset
│   └── it should accept the fill (AS-20 gate admits)
├── when collateralAsset decimals are 6 AND rollover output.amount is not aligned to the decimal offset
│   └── it should revert with DecimalTruncates
├── when collateralAsset decimals are 18 or greater
│   └── it should be a no-op regardless of rollover output.amount modulo (AS-20 early return)
├── when fillerData.outputIndex is 0 (rollover leg)
│   ├── when output.amount is not equal to orderSize
│   │   └── it should revert with PartialFillNotAllowed
│   ├── when fillRecords for rolloverOutputHash already set
│   │   └── it should revert with AlreadyFilled
│   ├── when intent hash mismatches orderData.cellarIntentHash
│   │   └── it should revert with IntentNotBoundToOrder
│   ├── when CellarIntent decodes and hashes to orderData.cellarIntentHash
│   │   ├── it should forward factory.executeIntentHooks with phase 0 and filler equal to msg.sender
│   │   ├── it should observe dstCstProduced via dstCST balance delta on the settler within 1-wei tolerance
│   │   ├── it should record FillRecord with filler msg.sender, dstCstProduced, and filledAt
│   │   ├── it should pull leftover srcCST from RolloverModule to msg.sender
│   │   └── it should not transition orderStatus
│   ├── when dstCstProduced plus 1 is less than fillSize minus leftover
│   │   └── it should revert with DisproportionateOutput
│   └── when dstCstProduced exceeds what would fit in uint128
│       └── it should record FillRecord.dstCstProduced at full uint256 width without narrowing (PR 3 / #53)
├── when fillerData.outputIndex is 1 (premium leg)
│   ├── when no rollover fill record exists for the order
│   │   └── it should revert with PremiumBeforeRollover
│   ├── when fillRecords for premiumOutputHash already set
│   │   └── it should revert with AlreadyFilled
│   ├── when debitFrom has insufficient ERC-6909 balance
│   │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance
│   ├── when debitFrom does not authorize msg.sender
│   │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedSettler
│   ├── when debitFrom authorizes msg.sender
│   │   └── it should debit requiredPremium via ERC6909.settle, forward factory.executeIntentHooks with phase 1 and filler equal to the rollover filler, flip paymentSettled to true while leaving orderStatus unchanged, and emit Fill for the premium output
│   ├── when requiredPremium is zero
│   │   └── it should short-circuit the ERC-6909 debit but still fire phase-1 hooks and flip paymentSettled
│   ├── when the cellar phase-1 premiumHooks revert after the ERC-6909 debit
│   │   └── it should emit PremiumHooksReverted, leave ERC-6909 debit and paymentSettled committed, and not revert (AS-10 / #58)
│   └── when a reentrant fill is attempted from inside premiumHooks
│       └── it should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall
└── when fillerData.outputIndex is neither 0 nor 1
    └── it should revert with InvalidOutputIndex
